Title: Run Queries
Section: Run Queries > Overview > Reading Nested and Composite Types

DuckDB supports nested and composite column types such as `LIST`, `STRUCT`, `MAP`, `UNION`, and `ENUM`. The JDBC driver maps each of these to an idiomatic Java object. Read the values from a `ResultSet` with `getObject`, which returns the following types:

Table:
- DuckDB type: `LIST`, `ARRAY` | Java type returned by `getObject`: `org.duckdb.DuckDBArray` (implements `java.sql.Array`)
- DuckDB type: `STRUCT` | Java type returned by `getObject`: `org.duckdb.DuckDBStruct` (implements `java.sql.Struct`)
- DuckDB type: `MAP` | Java type returned by `getObject`: `java.util.LinkedHashMap`
- DuckDB type: `UNION` | Java type returned by `getObject`: the resolved member value
- DuckDB type: `ENUM` | Java type returned by `getObject`: `String`

```java
